      "status": "completed",
      "finalText": "It's set up and switched on. From now on, anyone who submits the **Contact Us** form (frm_001) will go straight into the **New Lead Nurture** workflow (wf_001).\n\n- **Trigger:** \"Contact Us Form Submitted\" (trg_004). It was already there but turned off and not connected to any workflow. I connected it to New Lead Nurture and turned it on rather than making a duplicate.\n- **When it fires:** when a form is submitted and the form name is exactly \"Contact Us\".\n- **Workflow:** New Lead Nurture is already live. It sends a text, waits 1 day, then sends an email and creates a \"Call new lead\" task if the person hasn't replied.\n\n**Worth knowing:**\n- The trigger matches on the form's name. If the form is renamed, the trigger will stop firing until its condition is updated.\n- This only covers new submissions. The 3 people who already filled out the form won't be added.\n- The workflow starts with a text message. A run for one contact (con_008) failed at that step because they had opted out of texts. Anyone else without texts enabled may fail the same way.",
